COMMAND NAME: gppreupgrade

Checks for dependencies on the pg_stat_activity, pg_exttable, 
and pg_window system catalog relations prior to an upgrade.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

gppreupgrade [-d <master_data_directory>] [-l <logfile_directory>] 
[-D] [-?] [-v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
***************************************************** 

The gpdbupgrade utility needs to drop and recreate the 
pg_stat_activity, pg_exttable, and pg_window system catalog 
relations. If you have created objects that depend on these 
relations (such as views), you must drop them before you begin 
the upgrade process. 

Run this utility to check for dependencies on these catalog 
tables prior to upgrading. If dependent objects are found, you 
should secure a backup of the dependent object definitions and 
then drop the objects prior to upgrading. 

For example, to find the relevant view definitions, you can 
check the pg_views relation. For example:

psql -c "SELECT viewname, definition FROM pg_views \

              WHERE definition ILIKE '%pg_stat_activity%' \

              OR definition ILIKE '%pg_exttable%' \

              OR definition ILIKE '%pg_window%';" \

              >> views.out

After the upgrade is complete, you can use your saved object 
definitions to recreate the dependent objects.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The master host data directory. If not specified, 
the value set for $MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/gpAdminLogs.


-D (debug)

Sets logging level to debug.


-? (help)

Displays the online help.


-v (show script version)

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum 
of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Check for catalog dependencies prior to upgrade:

gppreupgrade


